; Stand in as the game's d3dx9_43.dll. EU4 imports D3DX9_43.DLL; Windows loads the game-directory
; copy before the System32 one (d3dx9_43.dll is NOT a KnownDLL -- checked), so our DllMain runs
; before the game's main and the mod is present in EVERY launch, Steam's included.
;
; Why d3dx9_43 and not version.dll/d3d9.dll: those two slots belong to the double-byte (CJK font)
; patches (EU4DLL and its kin), which load their plugin from the game directory at those names.
; d3dx9_43.dll is unclaimed on Steam as on Epic, and the exe imports exactly the eight names
; below (verified in eu4.exe's import table), so this proxy serves every import the loader binds.
;
; NO FORWARDERS. These used to read `= pgt_<real>_orig.<name>`, which meant the user had to
; hand-copy System32's real DLL into the game directory under a private name -- the most
; error-prone step in installing the mod, and one whose failure kills the process at load with no
; window and no log. The target could never simply be "d3dx9_43": the loader resolves a
; forwarder's module by the normal search order, finds US, and a self-referential forwarder is a
; load-time failure.
;
; Each name below is now a real exported stub (proxy.h) that jumps through a pointer filled during
; DllMain from the system copy, loaded by absolute path. One file to install instead of two.
LIBRARY per-good-trade
EXPORTS
    D3DXCompileShader
    D3DXCreateCubeTexture
    D3DXCreateLine
    D3DXCreateTexture
    D3DXLoadSurfaceFromMemory
    D3DXLoadSurfaceFromSurface
    D3DXSaveSurfaceToFileInMemory
    D3DXSaveTextureToFileInMemory
